BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall-o-ween  (Events listed below)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T210000
UID:bb7df1f2cbef8c0d84b19e2e20b4a3c7@wfhb.org
DESCRIPTION:9:30 am-12 pm: Buck’s Dead and Breakfast- Come create a spoo
 ky sweet treat at Buck’s Dead and Breakfast found in the Nature Center p
 arking lot. Please bring cash\, all proceeds go to Friends of McCormick’
 s Creek. Create a Spider Donuts $5. Hot Drinks $2. 10 am-12 pm: Pumpkin Ca
 rving- Carve a pumpkin and support the Friends of McCormick’s Creek. $5 
 cost per pumpkin. Please pay in cash and supplies are limited to the first
  50 guests. Meet at the Nature Center Amphitheater to begin. 3 pm-4 pm- Ss
 ssnakes- (Live Animals) Slither on over to our Nature Center Amphitheater 
 to learn about the longest snake of North America and the strongest predat
 ory snake in Indiana. Naturalist Kaitlyn will introduce you to our snake a
 mbassadors in this live animal program. 5:30 pm- 7:30 pm: Pumpkin Parade 
 – (Hike) Put on a costume and meet the Friends of McCormick’s Creek at
  the Nature Center to take a spooky hike through the woods to see Jack-o-L
 anterns from local artists. We will be on an accessible path for everyone 
 to enjoy. Vote on your favorite Jack-o-Lanterns and take a treat bag to go
 ! 8 pm-9 pm: Nocturnal Animal Show- (Live Animals) Come join WildCare to m
 eet some of their nocturnal animal ambassadors\, Silver Haired Bat and Sou
 thern Flying Squirrel. Discover the difference in these flying mammals! Pr
 ogram is being offered at the Nature Center Audiotorium.
LOCATION:Nature Center\, McCormick's Creek State Park\, 250 McCormick's Cr
 eek Park Road\, Spencer
URL:https://wfhb.org/events/fall-o-ween-events-listed-below/
X-SOURCE:WFHB Community Calendar
END:VEVENT
