DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T210000
UID:b1b4a348d13f2cc6257a02dfbb1aa1ee@wfhb.org
DESCRIPTION:An eye-opening and award-winning documentary about three survi
 vors of abuse fighting for their lives and how the legal system betrayed t
 hem. A panel discussion and Q&A will follow the screening with co-director
  Natalie Pattillo\, Kerry Hyatt Bennett (Chief Legal Counsel\, IN Coalitio
 n Against Domestic Violence)\, and Carrie Stillions (Executive Director\, 
 Middle Way House)\, moderated by Zoe Peterson (Senior Scientist\, Kinsey I
 nstitute\; Professor of Applied Psychology\, Education and Research Method
 ology).
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. Seventh Street \, Bloomington
URL:https://wfhb.org/events/film-and-so-i-stayed/
X-SOURCE:WFHB Community Calendar
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T200000
UID:7afa3eb110059a6b0a2f6f9d92c4be3d@wfhb.org
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist for a guided night hike on the Salt Cre
 ek Trail! The Full Moon is the brightest night of the month\, leading to i
 nteresting views along the creek. Learn about October’s full moon this y
 ear\, the Hunter’s Moon. The Salt Creek Trail is rated very easy\, but s
 hould be considered moderate in the dark. The trail has some minor slopes
 \, a short stretch of lawn\, and possible wet or icy spots depending on we
 ather. Our route is about 2 miles total and will take about an hour to com
 plete. Please do not bring pets on night hikes. Red flashlights are prefer
 red for night vision and can be loaned to hikers on request.
LOCATION:Olympic Pool parking lot\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashville
URL:https://wfhb.org/events/full-moon-hike/
X-SOURCE:WFHB Community Calendar
END:VEVENT
